  message: "**Pass-23 substrate measurements (F23.6, F23.8) extending WI-fagab's scope.**\n\n**(F23.6) qualified_name 0% gap is not Python-specific — extends to bash + javascript + solidity:**\n\n| Language | Internal nodes | qualified_name populated |\n|---|---|---|\n| python | 33,703 | 0 (0.0%) |\n| bash | 218 | **0 (0.0%)** |\n| typescript | 67 | 35 (52.2%) |\n| javascript | 13 | **0 (0.0%)** |\n| go | 9 | 5 (55.6%) |\n| rust | 9 | 5 (55.6%) |\n| solidity | 8 | **0 (0.0%)** |\n\nJavaScript's 0% is notable because `js_ts.py:_make_jsts_qualified_name()` is the very pattern this WI proposes Python should mirror — yet TS populates 52% and JS populates 0%. Either `_make_jsts_qualified_name` is invoked only on TS code paths (likely; the function may early-return for `.js`/`.jsx`), or the JS Symbol-construction sites haven't been updated to use it.\n\nbash (`bash.py`) and solidity (`solidity.py`) analyzers don't construct qualified_name at all.\n\n**Implication.** WI-fagab's \"fix py.py\" approach should widen to a per-analyzer kwarg sweep: py.py, bash.py, solidity.py, plus js_ts.py's JavaScript code-path. Or each language gets a peer face (sibling WIs under INV-jahiv). For minimum-viable closure of THIS WI, recommend keeping the title Python-focused and filing bash/javascript/solidity peers separately. For maximum cleanup, widen WI-fagab to cover all 4 and rename.\n\n**(F23.8) Python `docstring` 0% on `file`/`variable`/`call_site`/`external_symbol` kinds.** Python docstring coverage by node.kind:\n\n| kind | docstring populated |\n|---|---|\n| method | 13,660 / 18,268 (74.8%) |\n| function | 5,534 / 6,913 (80.1%) |\n| class | 3,987 / 4,437 (89.9%) |\n| variable | 0 / 1,608 (0.0%) |\n| file | 0 / 844 (0.0%) |\n| external_symbol | 0 / 1,504 (0.0%) |\n| call_site | 0 / 129 (0.0%) |\n\nModule-level docstrings on Python `file` nodes are routinely available (the project's own AGENTS.md mandates them: \"Each `.py` file should have a substantive module docstring\"). The Phase 4 sweep populated docstring for callables (function/method/class) but skipped file-level. Sibling concern to qualified_name on py.py — the analyzer wires some Symbol fields but not others.\n\n**Cluster.** F23.8 is more naturally a separate INV-jahiv residual (file/variable docstring coverage) than a WI-fagab face. Discussion entry here for traceability; if surfaced as a tracker item it can be a peer WI of WI-fagab and the new WI-bujot (is_exported).\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_0010_pass23.md`."  # 506b
